      "source_excerpt": "protocolSection.descriptionModule.detailedDescription; outcomesModule.primaryOutcomes and secondaryOutcomes: \"There will be 4 study visits during the study.\" \"At Visit 1 (baseline), patients will sign the informed consent and be assessed for mycological and clinical signs and symptoms of Tinea pedis.\" \"Patients will be issued with a tube of the cream and instructed to apply the cream sparingly to all affected areas of the foot (or feet), once daily (at night or in the evenings) for a total of 4 weeks according to protocol-specified guidelines.\" \"During the 4-week treatment period patients will return to the study every 2 weeks to be assessed for clinical signs and symptoms.\" \"After the 4-week treatment period, patients will continue participation in the study for an additional 2 weeks without medication.\" \"Patients will return then return to the study center for a final visit (Visit 4, Week 6) at which time skin scrapings will be sampled from interdigital spaces on both feet for KOH microscopy and mycological culture.\" \"The primary outcome measure in the study is a mycological cure (defined as negative KOH microscopy and negative mycological culture) at week 6.\" \"Week 6\" \"Week 6\" -- Visit weeks 2, 4 and 6 follow from assessment every 2 weeks during the 4-week treatment and the stated final Visit 4 at Week 6. Visit 1 is described as baseline, but no numeric baseline week is stated. The record describes four visits but does not provide a formal visit table.",
